>> title: Dinner Rolls
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, rolls, milk, butter, oven
>> counters: Bakery
>> pairs-with: pot-roast
>> servings: 12
>> time: 3 hr
>> slack: forgiving — the rolls come out when they are joined and golden, and five minutes past that dries the crumb the butter was meant to keep soft

>> step: stir, stand 10 min
Stir @warm whole milk{1%cup}(240 mL) with @granulated sugar{3%Tbs}(38 g) and @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), then let stand ~{10%min}.

>> step: beat in
Beat @egg{1%large} and @melted unsalted butter{5%Tbs}(70 g) into @&(~1)yeast mixture{}.

>> step: add flour and salt, knead 8 min
Add @all-purpose flour{3 1/2%cup}(420 g) and @table salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g) to @&(~1)wet mix{}, then knead ~{8%min}.

>> step: cover, rise until doubled
Cover @&(~1)dough{} and rise until doubled, ~{1%hour}.

>> step: divide into 12 balls, proof in a 9x13-in pan
Divide @&(~1)dough{} into 12 balls and proof in a #9x13-in pan{} for ~{45%min}.

>> step: brush, bake 375°F 20 min
Brush @&(~1)rolls{} with @melted salted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) and bake at 375°F for ~{20%min}.
